# The claude-workhorses hosts file: copy it to ~/.config/claude-workhorses/hosts and edit it.
# One host per line: name, ssh target, arch, cores, RAM in GB, profile, wallpaper color.
# - name: lower-case letters, digits and dashes; wh and sync.sh take it as the host's name.
# - ssh target: an alias from ~/.ssh/config or user@host. ~/.ssh/config decides the route.
# - arch: x86_64 or arm64. cores and RAM: whole numbers, shown to Claude in the host table.
# - profile: dedicated (the Mac is the workhorse's alone) or shared (its owner uses it too).
# - color: a dedicated host's solid-colour wallpaper, a file name from
#   /System/Library/Desktop Pictures/Solid Colors without .png; - on a shared host.
# The first host listed wins a tie when wh picks one by load.
alpha  alpha-mini             x86_64  6   16  dedicated  Turquoise Green
beta   beta-mini              x86_64  6   16  dedicated  Electric Blue
gamma  me@gamma.example.test  arm64   10  16  shared     -
